#!/usr/bin/env python3
# apply_trade_replay_live.py — ── TRADE_REPLAY_LIVE_20261017 ──
#
# Trade Replay on the Trades and Analytics pages, ADMIN ONLY.
#
#   backend  app/backtest/replay/live_replay.py      (new)  live/paper rows → replay payload + Kite corpus fill
#            app/api/live_replay_routes.py           (new)  GET /api/replay/trade?scope=trades|analytics&key=…
#            app/backtest/replay/test_live_replay.py (new)  behavioural suite (63 checks)
#            app/backtest/replay/replay_core.py      build_replay_for(run, …); open positions draw to now;
#                                                    a group is led by a leg of its opening minute
#            app/api_server.py                       router mounted behind _require_admin_ui
#   frontend components/replay/TradeReplay.jsx       fetchUrl / navKeys / sourceLabel props
#            pages/PaperTrades.jsx                   ▶ column (admin, fail-closed)
#            pages/Analytics.jsx                     ▶ on closed rows, open cards/table, condor cards
#
# Staged all-or-nothing: every anchor is checked (exactly once) and every
# Python file compiled BEFORE anything is written. After writing, both
# replay suites run (new 63 + existing 165) and the three JSX files are
# parsed with esbuild; any failure restores every file it touched.
#
#   cd <repo root> && python3 apply_trade_replay_live.py [repo_root] [--allow-dirty] [--skip-tests]
#   then: ./desktop/build-scalp.sh both   (deploy outside market hours — api_server.py changes)

